§ `Section 672.64 -- High-risk accused`

-- 672.64(1): on application made by the prosecutor before any disposition to discharge an accused absolutely, the court may, at the conclusion of a hearing, find the accused to be a high-risk accused if the accused has been found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder
-- for a serious personal injury offence, as defined in subsection 672.81(1.3), the accused was 18 years of age or more at the time of the commission of the offence and (a) the court is satisfied that there is a substantial likelihood that the accused will use violence that could endanger the life or safety of another person;
-- or (b) the court is of the opinion that the acts that constitute the offence were of such a brutal nature as to indicate a risk of grave physical or psychological harm to another person.
-- Two gates: the application before any discharge (a "where"-type gate: JUST FALSE, fork F-GRANT-WHERE) and the "if" conditions (NOTHING, fork F-GRANT-IF).
-- fork: F-GRANT-WHERE, F-GRANT-IF
-- src:13795 | 672.64 (1) On application made by the prosecutor before any disposition to discharge an accused absolutely, the court may, at the conclusion of a hearing, find the accused to be a high-risk accused if the accused has been found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for a serious personal injury offence, as defined in subsection 672.81(1.3), the accused was 18 years of age or more at the time of the commission of the offence and
-- src:13796 | (a) the court is satisfied that there is a substantial likelihood that the accused will use violence that could endanger the life or safety of another person; or
-- src:13797 | (b) the court is of the opinion that the acts that constitute the offence were of such a brutal nature as to indicate a risk of grave physical or psychological harm to another person.
@ref s 672.64(1); s 672.64(1)(a); s 672.64(1)(b) (src:13795-13797)
GIVEN `the prosecutor makes an application before any disposition to discharge the accused absolutely` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused has been found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for a serious personal injury offence, by s 672.81(1.3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the accused was 18 years of age or more at the time of the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that there is a substantial likelihood that the accused will use violence that could endanger the life or safety of another person` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
      `the court is of the opinion that the acts that constitute the offence were of such a brutal nature as to indicate a risk of grave physical or psychological harm to another person` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.64(1) the court may find the accused to be a high-risk accused` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the prosecutor makes an application before any disposition to discharge the accused absolutely` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On application made by the prosecutor before any disposition to discharge an accused absolutely"
        IF `the accused has been found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for a serious personal injury offence, by s 672.81(1.3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the accused was 18 years of age or more at the time of the commission of the offence` AND (`the court is satisfied that there is a substantial likelihood that the accused will use violence that could endanger the life or safety of another person` OR `the court is of the opinion that the acts that constitute the offence were of such a brutal nature as to indicate a risk of grave physical or psychological harm to another person`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the accused has been found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for a serious personal injury offence, as defined in subsection 672.81(1.3), the accused was 18 years of age or more at the time of the commission of the offence"

-- 672.64(2): in deciding whether to find that the accused is a high-risk accused, the court shall consider all relevant evidence, including (a) the nature and circumstances of the offence; (b) any pattern of repetitive behaviour of which the offence forms a part;
-- (c) the accused's current mental condition; (d) the past and expected course of the accused's treatment, including the accused's willingness to follow treatment; and (e) the opinions of experts who have examined the accused.
