§ `Sections 672.67 to 672.71 -- Dual status offenders`

-- 672.67(1): where a court imposes a sentence of imprisonment on an offender who is, or thereby becomes, a dual status offender, that sentence takes precedence over any prior custodial disposition, pending any placement decision by the Review Board.
-- 672.67(2): where a court imposes a custodial disposition on an accused who is, or thereby becomes, a dual status offender, the disposition takes precedence over any prior sentence of imprisonment pending any placement decision by the Review Board.
-- src:13817 | 672.67 (1) Where a court imposes a sentence of imprisonment on an offender who is, or thereby becomes, a dual status offender, that sentence takes precedence over any prior custodial disposition, pending any placement decision by the Review Board.
-- src:13818 | Custodial disposition by court
-- src:13819 | (2) Where a court imposes a custodial disposition on an accused who is, or thereby becomes, a dual status offender, the disposition takes precedence over any prior sentence of imprisonment pending any placement decision by the Review Board.
@ref s 672.67(1); s 672.67(2) (src:13817-13819)
DECLARE `s 672.67 which takes precedence` IS ONE OF
    `s 672.67(1) the new sentence of imprisonment takes precedence over any prior custodial disposition`
    `s 672.67(2) the new custodial disposition takes precedence over any prior sentence of imprisonment`
    `s 672.67 the Review Board has made a placement decision and precedence is for it to say`
    `s 672.67 not covered`

@ref s 672.67(1); s 672.67(2) (src:13817-13819)
GIVEN `the person is, or thereby becomes, a dual status offender, by s 672.1(1) dual status offender` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a court imposes a sentence of imprisonment on the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a court imposes a custodial disposition on the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Review Board has made a placement decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 672.67 which takes precedence`
`s 672.67 which of the two takes precedence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is, or thereby becomes, a dual status offender, by s 672.1(1) dual status offender` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN `s 672.67 not covered`   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offender who is, or thereby becomes, a dual status offender"
        IF `the Review Board has made a placement decision` THEN `s 672.67 the Review Board has made a placement decision and precedence is for it to say`   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "pending any placement decision by the Review Board"
        IF `a court imposes a sentence of imprisonment on the offender` THEN `s 672.67(1) the new sentence of imprisonment takes precedence over any prior custodial disposition`
        IF `a court imposes a custodial disposition on the accused` THEN `s 672.67(2) the new custodial disposition takes precedence over any prior sentence of imprisonment`
        OTHERWISE `s 672.67 not covered`   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the court has imposed neither a sentence of imprisonment nor a custodial disposition

