-- 672.68(4): the Review Board shall make its placement decision as soon as practicable but not later than thirty days after receiving an application from, or giving notice to, the Minister under subsection (2),
-- unless the Review Board and the Minister agree to a longer period not exceeding sixty days. As a regulative rule: the Review Board's duty, within 30 days.
-- src:13832 | (4) The Review Board shall make its placement decision as soon as practicable but not later than thirty days after receiving an application from, or giving notice to, the Minister under subsection (2), unless the Review Board and the Minister agree to a longer period not exceeding sixty days.
@ref s 672.68(4) (src:13832)
DECLARE `s 672.68(4) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 672.68(4) make the placement decision`

@ref s 672.68(4) (src:13832)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 672.68(4) act`
`s 672.68(4) the Review Board must make its placement decision within thirty days` MEANS
    PARTY `a Review Board`
    MUST `s 672.68(4) make the placement decision`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `a Review Board` BECAUSE "no placement decision was made within thirty days after receiving an application from, or giving notice to, the Minister"

-- The same duty as a decision function over dates; the longer period the Review Board and the Minister may agree is an input (not exceeding sixty days).
-- fork: F-MUST-BARE, F-UNLESS-MET
@ref s 672.68(4) (src:13832)
GIVEN `the day the Review Board receives an application from, or gives notice to, the Minister under subsection 672.68(2)` IS A DATE
      `the day the Review Board makes its placement decision` IS A DATE
      `the Review Board and the Minister agree to a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the longer period agreed, in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.68(4) the placement decision is made in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the day the Review Board makes its placement decision` AT MOST (`the day the Review Board receives an application from, or gives notice to, the Minister under subsection 672.68(2)` PLUS 30) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the Review Board and the Minister agree to a longer period` AND `the longer period agreed, in days` AT MOST 60 AND `the day the Review Board makes its placement decision` AT MOST (`the day the Review Board receives an application from, or gives notice to, the Minister under subsection 672.68(2)` PLUS `the longer period agreed, in days`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not later than thirty days after receiving an application from, or giving notice to, the Minister under subsection (2), unless the Review Board and the Minister agree to a longer period not exceeding sixty days"

