-- 672.71(2): when a dual status offender is convicted or discharged on the conditions set out in a probation order made under section 730 in respect of an offence but is not sentenced to a term of imprisonment, the custodial disposition in respect of the accused comes into force and,
-- notwithstanding subsection 732.2(1), takes precedence over any probation order made in respect of the offence.
